  "result": "All 5 tests pass.\n\n**What I did:** Implemented `ledger/ledger.py` with the `Ledger` class and the `InsufficientFunds` and `UnknownAccount` exceptions per the spec. Amounts are validated as non-negative integers, duplicate account ids raise `ValueError`, and `transfer` checks both accounts and the source balance before mutating anything, so a failed transfer leaves both balances untouched.\n\n**Approach:** I chose Approach B (snapshot state). The spec's public interface exposes only current balances, with no history, replay, or time-travel methods, so a plain id-to-balance mapping satisfies every requirement with the least code and no derived-state cache to keep consistent.",
